IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa27-definitions`
IMPORT `coa27-ch4-register`

-- coa27-ch6-second-audit-offences.l4: Companies Act 2006 (United Kingdom), Part 42 Chapter 6 (part): ss 1248 to 1250
-- (second company audit; false and misleading statements) and ss 1255 to 1257 (offences by bodies corporate,
-- time limits, jurisdiction), lines 17648-17698 and 17883-17908 of ukpga-2006-46.txt.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively); part agent coa27.
--
-- READING A RESULT (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer): JUST TRUE the text says yes; JUST FALSE
-- the text says no in its own words ("if", "where", "unless", "does not authorise", a defence not shown); NOTHING the
-- text does not decide (silent, limited by its own wording, points outside the text). A caller never turns NOTHING
-- into FALSE. Two shapes of offence sentence are answered differently on purpose and listed in NOTES.md:
--   "A person is guilty of an offence if ..."  (s 1248(5), (7); s 1250(1))   -> JUST FALSE when the "if" fails;
--   "It is an offence for a person ... to ..."  (s 1250(2)-(4))              -> JUST TRUE or NOTHING, never FALSE.
-- AMOUNTS. The pounds a level on the standard scale stands for, "the statutory maximum" and "the general limit in a
-- magistrates' court" are not in the Act: they are INPUTS, never a number from memory.
-- DATES. "within the period of 21 days beginning with the date on which it is given" counts the date given as day one,
-- so the last day is the date given plus 20. "within 12 months beginning with the date" ends the day before the
-- corresponding date a year later (a leap-day start ends on 28 February: NOTES.md, fork register).
-- Every name begins with the section label it implements.

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1248 Secretary of State's power to require second audit of a company
-- =========================================================================================================

-- The facts about a person appointed as statutory auditor of a company that the definition of "appropriate" reads.
DECLARE `s 1248(3) person` HAS
    `s 1248(3) is an Auditor General` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1248(3) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1248(3) is eligible for appointment as statutory auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 1248(3) is prohibited by section 1214(1) from acting as statutory auditor of the company (the independence requirement: a seam answer)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN

-- src:17655 | (3) For the purposes of subsections (1) and (2) a person is “appropriate” if he—
-- src:17656 | (a) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor or, if the person is an Auditor General, for appointment as statutory auditor of the company, and
-- src:17657 | (b) is not prohibited by section 1214(1) (independence requirement) from acting as statutory auditor of the company.
@ref s 1248(3) Second audit: "appropriate" (src:17655-17657)
GIVEN p IS A `s 1248(3) person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1248(3) the person is appropriate` MEANS
    IF NOT (IF p's `s 1248(3) is an Auditor General`
            THEN p's `s 1248(3) is eligible for appointment as statutory auditor of the company`
            ELSE p's `s 1248(3) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person is “appropriate” if he (a) is eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor"
    ELSE CONSIDER p's `s 1248(3) is prohibited by section 1214(1) from acting as statutory auditor of the company (the independence requirement: a seam answer)`
         WHEN JUST x THEN
             IF x
             THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) is not prohibited by section 1214(1) (independence requirement) from acting as statutory auditor of the company"
             ELSE JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer under section 1214(1) belongs to another part (a seam)

-- src:17651 | (1) This section applies where a person appointed as statutory auditor of a company was not an appropriate person for any part of the period during which the audit was conducted.
@ref s 1248(1) Second audit: when the section applies (src:17651-17651)
GIVEN `a person appointed as statutory auditor of the company was not an appropriate person for any part of the period during which the audit was conducted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1248(1) this section applies` MEANS
    IF `a person appointed as statutory auditor of the company was not an appropriate person for any part of the period during which the audit was conducted`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where"

-- src:17652 | (2) The Secretary of State may direct the company concerned to retain an appropriate person—
-- src:17653 | (a) to conduct a second audit of the relevant accounts, or
-- src:17654 | (b) to review the first audit and to report (giving his reasons) whether a second audit is needed.
@ref s 1248(2) Second audit: the direction (src:17652-17654)
GIVEN `this section applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1248(2) the Secretary of State may direct the company to retain an appropriate person` MEANS
    IF `this section applies`
    THEN JUST TRUE -- (a) to conduct a second audit of the relevant accounts, or (b) to review the first audit and report whether a second audit is needed
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies where" (subsection (1)); the power in (2) is exercised only in that case

-- src:17658 | (4) The Secretary of State must send a copy of a direction under subsection (2) to the registrar of companies.
@ref s 1248(4) Second audit: copy to the registrar (src:17658-17658)
GIVEN `a direction has been given under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1248(4) the Secretary of State must send a copy of the direction to the registrar of companies` MEANS
    IF `a direction has been given under subsection (2)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a copy of a direction under subsection (2)"

-- ---- s 1248(5): the company's offence for failing to comply with the direction -----------------------------

-- src:17660 | (a) it fails to comply with a direction under subsection (2) within the period of 21 days beginning with the date on which it is given, or
@ref s 1248(5)(a) Second audit: the period of 21 days (src:17660-17660)
GIVEN `the date the direction was given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1248(5)(a) the last day of the period of 21 days beginning with the date the direction is given` MEANS
    `the date the direction was given` PLUS 20 -- the date given is the first of the 21 days

@ref s 1248(5)(a) Second audit: failure to comply within the 21 days (src:17660-17660)
GIVEN `the date the direction was given` IS A DATE
      `the date the company complied with the direction (NOTHING if it has not)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1248(5)(a) the company fails to comply with the direction within the period of 21 days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the company complied with the direction (NOTHING if it has not)`
    WHEN JUST d THEN d GREATER THAN `s 1248(5)(a) the last day of the period of 21 days beginning with the date the direction is given` `the date the direction was given`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date as at which the question is asked` GREATER THAN `s 1248(5)(a) the last day of the period of 21 days beginning with the date the direction is given` `the date the direction was given`

-- src:17661 | (b) it has been convicted of a previous offence under this subsection and the failure to comply with the direction which led to the conviction continues after the conviction.
@ref s 1248(5)(b) Second audit: continued failure after a conviction (src:17661-17661)
GIVEN `the company has been convicted of a previous offence under subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure to comply with the direction which led to the conviction continues after the conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1248(5)(b) the failure continues after a previous conviction` MEANS
    `the company has been convicted of a previous offence under subsection (5)`
    AND `the failure to comply with the direction which led to the conviction continues after the conviction`

-- src:17659 | (5) The company is guilty of an offence if—
-- src:17660 | (a) it fails to comply with a direction under subsection (2) within the period of 21 days beginning with the date on which it is given, or
-- src:17661 | (b) it has been convicted of a previous offence under this subsection and the failure to comply with the direction which led to the conviction continues after the conviction.
@ref s 1248(5) Second audit: the company's offence (src:17659-17661)
GIVEN `the failure within paragraph (a) has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure within paragraph (b) has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1248(5) the company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the failure within paragraph (a) has occurred` OR `the failure within paragraph (b) has occurred`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company is guilty of an offence if"

-- ---- s 1248(6) and (7): the report, and the company's offences -------------------------------------------

-- src:17662 | (6) The company must—
-- src:17663 | (a) send a copy of a report under subsection (2)(b) to the registrar of companies, and
-- src:17664 | (b) if the report states that a second audit is needed, take such steps as are necessary for the carrying out of that audit.
@ref s 1248(6) Second audit: the company's duties after a report (src:17662-17664)
GIVEN `a report has been given under subsection (2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1248(6)(a) the company must send a copy of the report to the registrar of companies` MEANS
    IF `a report has been given under subsection (2)(b)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a copy of a report under subsection (2)(b)"

@ref s 1248(6) Second audit: the company's duties after a report (src:17662-17664)
GIVEN `the report states that a second audit is needed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1248(6)(b) the company must take the steps necessary for the carrying out of the second audit` MEANS
    IF `the report states that a second audit is needed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the report states that a second audit is needed"

-- src:17666 | (a) it fails to send a copy of a report under subsection (2)(b) to the registrar within the period of 21 days beginning with the date on which it receives it,
@ref s 1248(7)(a) Second audit: failure to send the report within 21 days (src:17666-17666)
GIVEN `the date the company received the report` IS A DATE
      `the date the company sent a copy of the report to the registrar (NOTHING if it has not)` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date as at which the question is asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1248(7)(a) the company fails to send a copy of the report to the registrar within the period of 21 days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the company sent a copy of the report to the registrar (NOTHING if it has not)`
    WHEN JUST d THEN d GREATER THAN (`the date the company received the report` PLUS 20)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date as at which the question is asked` GREATER THAN (`the date the company received the report` PLUS 20)

-- src:17667 | (b) in a case within subsection (6)(b), it fails to take the steps mentioned immediately it receives the report, or
@ref s 1248(7)(b) Second audit: failure to take the steps immediately (src:17667-17667)
GIVEN `the report states that a second audit is needed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company took the steps mentioned immediately it received the report` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1248(7)(b) the company fails to take the steps immediately it receives the report` MEANS
    `the report states that a second audit is needed` AND (NOT `the company took the steps mentioned immediately it received the report`)

-- src:17668 | (c) it has been convicted of a previous offence under this subsection and the failure to send a copy of the report, or take the steps, which led to the conviction continues after the conviction.
@ref s 1248(7)(c) Second audit: continued failure after a previous conviction (src:17668-17668)
GIVEN `the company has been convicted of a previous offence under subsection (7)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure to send the copy of the report, or take the steps, which led to the conviction continues after the conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1248(7)(c) the failure continues after a previous conviction` MEANS
    `the company has been convicted of a previous offence under subsection (7)`
    AND `the failure to send the copy of the report, or take the steps, which led to the conviction continues after the conviction`

-- src:17665 | (7) The company is guilty of an offence if—
-- src:17666 | (a) it fails to send a copy of a report under subsection (2)(b) to the registrar within the period of 21 days beginning with the date on which it receives it,
-- src:17667 | (b) in a case within subsection (6)(b), it fails to take the steps mentioned immediately it receives the report, or
-- src:17668 | (c) it has been convicted of a previous offence under this subsection and the failure to send a copy of the report, or take the steps, which led to the conviction continues after the conviction.
@ref s 1248(7) Second audit: the company's offence (src:17665-17668)
GIVEN `the failure within paragraph (a) has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure within paragraph (b) has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure within paragraph (c) has occurred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1248(7) the company is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the failure within paragraph (a) has occurred` OR `the failure within paragraph (b) has occurred` OR `the failure within paragraph (c) has occurred`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company is guilty of an offence if"

-- ---- s 1248(8): the penalty ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- THE TEXT CARRIES TWO EXTENTS OF (8)(b), run together in the rendering: "...one-tenth of level 5 on the standard
-- scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale for each day on which the failure
-- continues." Both are encoded. The combining function answers NOTHING when they differ (silent: the text does not say
-- which extent is in force). NEEDS-CORE.md records the fine the core cannot say.

DECLARE `s 1248(8) case` IS ONE OF
    `s 1248(5)(a) failure to comply with the direction within 21 days`
    `s 1248(5)(b) continued failure to comply after a previous conviction`
    `s 1248(7)(a) failure to send the copy of the report within 21 days`
    `s 1248(7)(b) failure to take the steps immediately`
    `s 1248(7)(c) continued failure to send the copy or take the steps after a previous conviction`

-- src:17669 | (8) A company guilty of an offence under this section is liable on summary conviction—
-- src:17670 | (a) in a case within subsection (5)(a) or (7)(a) or (b), to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale, and
-- src:17671 | (b) in a case within subsection (5)(b) or (7)(c), to a fine not exceeding one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scaleone-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale for each day on which the failure continues.
@ref s 1248(8) Second audit: penalty on summary conviction (src:17669-17671)
GIVEN c IS A `s 1248(8) case`
GIVETH A `Penalty`
`s 1248(8) the penalty on the first extent of the text for` MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `s 1248(5)(a) failure to comply with the direction within 21 days` THEN
        Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                   , `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                   , `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
                   , `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                   , `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
    WHEN `s 1248(7)(a) failure to send the copy of the report within 21 days` THEN
        Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                   , `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                   , `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
                   , `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                   , `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
    WHEN `s 1248(7)(b) failure to take the steps immediately` THEN
        Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                   , `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                   , `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
                   , `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                   , `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
    -- (b): "for each day on which the failure continues": the core's daily slot carries the per-day fine, although the text
    -- does not use the words "daily default fine" (NOTES.md, finding)
    WHEN `s 1248(5)(b) continued failure to comply after a previous conviction` THEN
        Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                   , `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                   , `fine not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                   , `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1)
                   , `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE
    WHEN `s 1248(7)(c) continued failure to send the copy or take the steps after a previous conviction` THEN
        Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction`
                   , `imprisonment not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                   , `fine not exceeding` IS NOTHING
                   , `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 0.1)
                   , `imprisonment and fine together` IS FALSE

@ref s 1248(8)(b) Second audit: the daily fine on the first extent (src:17671-17671)
GIVEN `the amount level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1248(8)(b) the daily fine on the first extent in pounds` MEANS
    `the amount level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` TIMES 0.1 -- one-tenth of level 5 on the standard scale

@ref s 1248(8)(b) Second audit: the daily fine on the second extent (src:17671-17671)
GIVEN `the amount level 4 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 1248(8)(b) the daily fine on the second extent in pounds` MEANS
    (IF `the amount level 4 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` GREATER THAN 5000
     THEN `the amount level 4 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds`
     ELSE 5000) TIMES 0.1 -- one-tenth of the greater of £5,000 or level 4 on the standard scale

@ref s 1248(8)(b) Second audit: the daily fine, both extents (src:17671-17671)
GIVEN `the amount level 4 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 1248(8)(b) the maximum daily fine in pounds` MEANS
    IF `s 1248(8)(b) the daily fine on the first extent in pounds` `the amount level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds`
       EQUALS `s 1248(8)(b) the daily fine on the second extent in pounds` `the amount level 4 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds`
    THEN JUST (`s 1248(8)(b) the daily fine on the first extent in pounds` `the amount level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text carries two extents of paragraph (b) and does not say which is in force

@ref s 1248(8) Second audit: the maximum fine for the case (src:17669-17671)
GIVEN c IS A `s 1248(8) case`
      `the amount level 4 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 1248(8) the maximum fine in pounds for` MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `s 1248(5)(a) failure to comply with the direction within 21 days` THEN JUST `the amount level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds`
    WHEN `s 1248(7)(a) failure to send the copy of the report within 21 days` THEN JUST `the amount level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds`
    WHEN `s 1248(7)(b) failure to take the steps immediately` THEN JUST `the amount level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds`
    WHEN `s 1248(5)(b) continued failure to comply after a previous conviction` THEN
        `s 1248(8)(b) the maximum daily fine in pounds` `the amount level 4 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` `the amount level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds`
    WHEN `s 1248(7)(c) continued failure to send the copy or take the steps after a previous conviction` THEN
        `s 1248(8)(b) the maximum daily fine in pounds` `the amount level 4 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` `the amount level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds`

GIVEN c IS A `s 1248(8) case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1248(8) the fine is for each day on which the failure continues` MEANS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `s 1248(5)(b) continued failure to comply after a previous conviction` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 1248(7)(c) continued failure to send the copy or take the steps after a previous conviction` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:17672 | (9) In this section “registrar of companies” has the meaning given by section 1060.
@ref s 1248(9) Second audit: "registrar of companies" (src:17672-17672)
GIVEN `the person is the registrar of companies within the meaning given by section 1060` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1248(9) the person is the registrar of companies` MEANS
    `the person is the registrar of companies within the meaning given by section 1060`
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) whenever the input is NOTHING: the meaning is given by s 1060 (coa23)

-- ---- regulative twins: the two 21-day duties, as the text puts them -----------------------------------------
-- THE UNIT IS DAYS, AND ONLY THIS COMMENT SAYS SO. #TRACE time 0 is the date on which the direction is given (or the
-- report received): the first of the 21 days. "Within the period of 21 days beginning with" that date therefore ends at
-- time 20. The stable binary cannot #ASSERT on a deontic value (it reports "unsupported-equality"), so the same two
-- tests are asserted on the twin decision functions above (s 1248(5)(a), s 1248(7)(a)).
DECLARE `s 1248 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 1248 comply with the direction under subsection (2)`
    `s 1248 send a copy of the report to the registrar of companies`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 1248 act`
`s 1248(5)(a) the company must comply with the direction` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 1248 comply with the direction under subsection (2)`
    WITHIN 20
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not comply with the direction within the period of 21 days beginning with the date on which it was given"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 1248 act`
`s 1248(7)(a) the company must send a copy of the report to the registrar` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    MUST `s 1248 send a copy of the report to the registrar of companies`
    WITHIN 20
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "the company did not send a copy of the report to the registrar within the period of 21 days beginning with the date on which it received it"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1249 Supplementary provision about second audits
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17674 | (1) If a person accepts an appointment, or continues to act, as statutory auditor of a company at a time when he knows he is not an appropriate person, the company may recover from him any costs incurred by it in complying with the requirements of section 1248.
-- src:17675 | For this purpose “appropriate” is to be construed in accordance with subsection (3) of that section.
@ref s 1249(1) Second audits: recovery of costs (src:17674-17675)
GIVEN p IS A `s 1248(3) person`
      `the person accepts an appointment, or continues to act, as statutory auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows he is not an appropriate person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1249(1) the company may recover from the person the costs it incurred in complying with section 1248` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the person accepts an appointment, or continues to act, as statutory auditor of the company` AND `the person knows he is not an appropriate person`)
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a person accepts an appointment, or continues to act, as statutory auditor of a company at a time when he knows he is not an appropriate person, the company may recover from him" (name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q2)
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1248(3) the person is appropriate` p
         WHEN JUST a THEN
             IF a
             THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the person is appropriate, so he cannot "know he is not an appropriate person" (name test of 2026-11-12, fork F-Q2)
             ELSE JUST TRUE
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether he is appropriate turns on section 1214(1), which belongs to another part (a seam)

@ref s 1249(1) Second audits: the amount recoverable (src:17674-17675)
GIVEN `the company may recover its costs from the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the costs incurred by the company in complying with the requirements of section 1248, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 1249(1) the amount the company may recover from the person` MEANS
    IF `the company may recover its costs from the person`
    THEN JUST `the costs incurred by the company in complying with the requirements of section 1248, in pounds`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the company may recover from him any costs incurred by it"; with no right to recover there is no amount to state (not 0, which would read as "£0 of costs")

-- src:17676 | (2) Where a second audit is carried out under section 1248, any statutory or other provision applying in relation to the first audit applies also, in so far as practicable, in relation to the second audit.
@ref s 1249(2) Second audits: provisions applying to the first audit (src:17676-17676)
GIVEN `the provision applies in relation to the first audit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is practicable for it to apply in relation to the second audit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1249(2) the provision applies also in relation to the second audit` MEANS
    IF `the provision applies in relation to the first audit` AND `it is practicable for it to apply in relation to the second audit`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in so far as practicable"

-- src:17677 | (3) A direction under section 1248(2) is, on the application of the Secretary of State, enforceable by injunction or, in Scotland, by an order under section 45 of the Court of Session Act 1988 (c. 36).
@ref s 1249(3) Second audits: enforcement of a direction (src:17677-17677)
GIVEN `the direction is a direction under section 1248(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary of State has applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceedings are in Scotland` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 1239(8) remedy`
`s 1249(3) the direction is enforceable by` MEANS
    IF `the direction is a direction under section 1248(2)` AND `the Secretary of State has applied`
    THEN
        IF `the proceedings are in Scotland`
        THEN JUST `s 1239(8) an order under section 45 of the Court of Session Act 1988`
        ELSE JUST `s 1239(8) an injunction`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A direction under section 1248(2) is, on the application of the Secretary of State, enforceable"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1250 Misleading, false and deceptive statements
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17680 | (1) A person is guilty of an offence if—
-- src:17681 | (a) for the purposes of or in connection with any application under this Part, or
-- src:17682 | (b) in purported compliance with any requirement imposed on him by or by virtue of this Part,
-- src:17683 | he knowingly or recklessly furnishes information which is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular.
@ref s 1250(1) False statements: the offence (src:17680-17683)
GIVEN `the information was furnished for the purposes of or in connection with an application under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information was furnished in purported compliance with a requirement imposed on him by or by virtue of this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he furnished it knowingly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he furnished it recklessly` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1250(1) the person is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF       (`the information was furnished for the purposes of or in connection with an application under this Part`
              OR `the information was furnished in purported compliance with a requirement imposed on him by or by virtue of this Part`)
         AND (`he furnished it knowingly` OR `he furnished it recklessly`)
         AND `the information is misleading, false or deceptive in a material particular`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person is guilty of an offence if"

-- src:17684 | (2) It is an offence for a person whose name does not appear on the register of auditors kept under regulations under section 1239 in an entry made under subsection (1)(a) of that section to describe himself as a registered auditor or so to hold himself out as to indicate, or be reasonably understood to indicate, that he is a registered auditor.
@ref s 1250(2) False statements: holding out as a registered auditor (src:17684-17684)
GIVEN `the person's name does not appear on the register of auditors in an entry made under section 1239(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he describes himself as a registered auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he so holds himself out as to indicate, or be reasonably understood to indicate, that he is a registered auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1250(2) the person commits an offence by describing himself as a registered auditor` MEANS
    IF       `the person's name does not appear on the register of auditors in an entry made under section 1239(1)(a)`
         AND (`he describes himself as a registered auditor` OR `he so holds himself out as to indicate, or be reasonably understood to indicate, that he is a registered auditor`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is an offence for a person whose name does not appear on the register ... to describe himself as a registered auditor or so to hold himself out"

-- src:17685 | (3) It is an offence for a person whose name does not appear on the register of auditors kept under regulations under that section in an entry made under subsection (1)(b) of that section to describe himself as a registered third country auditor or so to hold himself out as to indicate, or be reasonably understood to indicate, that he is a registered third country auditor.
@ref s 1250(3) False statements: holding out as a registered third country auditor (src:17685-17685)
GIVEN `the person's name does not appear on the register of auditors in an entry made under section 1239(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he describes himself as a registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he so holds himself out as to indicate, or be reasonably understood to indicate, that he is a registered third country auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1250(3) the person commits an offence by describing himself as a registered third country auditor` MEANS
    IF       `the person's name does not appear on the register of auditors in an entry made under section 1239(1)(b)`
         AND (`he describes himself as a registered third country auditor` OR `he so holds himself out as to indicate, or be reasonably understood to indicate, that he is a registered third country auditor`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is an offence for a person whose name does not appear on the register ... to describe himself as a registered third country auditor or so to hold himself out"

-- src:17686 | (4) It is an offence for a body which is not a recognised supervisory body or a recognised qualifying body to describe itself as so recognised or so to describe itself or hold itself out as to indicate, or be reasonably understood to indicate, that it is so recognised.
@ref s 1250(4) False statements: holding out as a recognised body (src:17686-17686)
GIVEN `the body is not a recognised supervisory body or a recognised qualifying body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it describes itself as so recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it so describes itself or holds itself out as to indicate, or be reasonably understood to indicate, that it is so recognised` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1250(4) the body commits an offence by describing itself as a recognised body` MEANS
    IF       `the body is not a recognised supervisory body or a recognised qualifying body`
         AND (`it describes itself as so recognised` OR `it so describes itself or holds itself out as to indicate, or be reasonably understood to indicate, that it is so recognised`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "It is an offence for a body which is not a recognised supervisory body or a recognised qualifying body to describe itself as so recognised"

-- The penalties. Section 1250(5)(b)(i) gives the English and Welsh maximum term as "the general limit in a magistrates'
-- court", a figure outside the Act: an INPUT, in months. THE TEXT'S OWN LEFTOVER (src:17692): "In relation to an offence
-- committed before 2 May 2022, for “twelve months” in paragraph (b)(i) substitute “six months”." Paragraph (b)(i) as
-- printed no longer contains "twelve months", so the substitution cannot be made word for word. It is read as meant:
-- six months for an offence committed before 2 May 2022 (fork F-A in NOTES.md).

-- src:17687 | (5) A person guilty of an offence under subsection (1) is liable—
-- src:17688 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or to a fine (or both);
-- src:17689 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:17690 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both),
-- src:17691 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
-- src:17692 | In relation to an offence committed before 2 May 2022, for “twelve months” in paragraph (b)(i) substitute “six months”.
@ref s 1250(5) False statements: penalty for an offence under subsection (1) (src:17687-17692)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE
      `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1250(5) the penalty for an offence under subsection (1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on conviction on indictment`
                         , `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 2, Years)
                         , `fine not exceeding` IS JUST `a fine without a stated limit`
                         , `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                         , `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
                         , `imprisonment not exceeding` IS
                               JUST (Period OF (IF `the date the offence was committed` LESS THAN (Date 2 5 2022)
                                                THEN 6
                                                ELSE `the general limit in a magistrates' court, in months`), Months)
                         , `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1)
                         , `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                         , `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
                         , `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 6, Months)
                         , `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1)
                         , `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                         , `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
                         , `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 6, Months)
                         , `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` OF 1)
                         , `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                         , `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (b) distinguishes England and Wales from Scotland and Northern Ireland

-- src:17693 | (6) Subject to subsection (7), a person guilty of an offence under subsection (2), (3) or (4) is liable on summary conviction—
-- src:17694 | (a) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 51 weeks or to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale (or both),
-- src:17695 | (b) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale (or both).
-- src:17696 | In relation to an offence committed before the commencement of section 281(5) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003, for “51 weeks” in paragraph (a) substitute “six months”.
@ref s 1250(6) False statements: penalty for an offence under subsection (2), (3) or (4) (src:17693-17696)
GIVEN mode IS A `Mode of conviction`
      `the offence was committed before the commencement of section 281(5) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 1250(6) the penalty for an offence under subsection (2), (3) or (4)` MEANS
    CONSIDER mode
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in England and Wales`
                         , `imprisonment not exceeding` IS
                               IF `the offence was committed before the commencement of section 281(5) of the Criminal Justice Act 2003`
                               THEN JUST (Period OF 6, Months)
                               ELSE JUST (Period OF 51, Weeks)
                         , `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
                         , `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                         , `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Scotland`
                         , `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 6, Months)
                         , `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
                         , `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                         , `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
        JUST (Penalty WITH `how convicted` IS `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`
                         , `imprisonment not exceeding` IS JUST (Period OF 6, Months)
                         , `fine not exceeding` IS JUST (`a fine not exceeding a level on the standard scale` OF 5, 1)
                         , `daily default fine for continued contravention` IS NOTHING
                         , `imprisonment and fine together` IS TRUE)
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "is liable on summary conviction"
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraphs (a) and (b) distinguish England and Wales from Scotland and Northern Ireland

-- src:17697 | (7) Where a contravention of subsection (2), (3) or (4) involves a public display of the offending description, the maximum fine that may be imposed is an amount equal to level 5 on the standard scale multiplied by the number of days for which the display has continued.
@ref s 1250(7) False statements: public display (src:17697-17697)
GIVEN `the contravention involves a public display of the offending description` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of days for which the display has continued` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 1250(7) the maximum fine that may be imposed` MEANS
    IF `the contravention involves a public display of the offending description`
    THEN JUST (`the amount level 5 on the standard scale stands for, in pounds` TIMES `the number of days for which the display has continued`)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where a contravention of subsection (2), (3) or (4) involves a public display"; otherwise subsection (6)'s level 5 applies

-- src:17698 | (8) It is a defence for a person charged with an offence under subsection (2), (3) or (4) to show that he took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence.
@ref s 1250(8) False statements: defence (src:17698-17698)
GIVEN `the person is charged with an offence under subsection (2), (3) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he shows that he took all reasonable precautions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he shows that he exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1250(8) the section gives the person a defence` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is charged with an offence under subsection (2), (3) or (4)`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a defence for a person charged with an offence under subsection (2), (3) or (4)"
    ELSE IF `he shows that he took all reasonable precautions` AND `he shows that he exercised all due diligence to avoid the commission of the offence`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is a defence ... to show that he took all reasonable precautions and exercised all due diligence": this section gives no defence on these facts (the ruling of 2026-11-05 (b))

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1255 Offences by bodies corporate, partnerships and unincorporated associations
-- =========================================================================================================

-- src:17885 | (1) Where an offence under this Part committed by a body corporate is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of, or to be attributable to any neglect on the part of, an officer of the body, or a person purporting to act in any such capacity, he as well as the body corporate is guilty of the offence and liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
@ref s 1255(1) Offences by bodies corporate: the officer (src:17885-17885)
GIVEN `the offence under this Part was committed by a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the offence was committed with the consent or connivance of the officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person purports to act as an officer of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the body corporate (s 1261(1))` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1255(1) the officer is guilty of the offence as well as the body corporate` MEANS
    IF       NOT (`the offence under this Part was committed by a body corporate`
                  AND (`it is proved that the offence was committed with the consent or connivance of the officer`
                       OR `it is proved that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the officer`))
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence under this Part committed by a body corporate is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of, or to be attributable to any neglect on the part of, an officer"
    ELSE IF `the person purports to act as an officer of the body`
         THEN JUST TRUE -- "or a person purporting to act in any such capacity"
         ELSE `the person is an officer of the body corporate (s 1261(1))`
              -- JUST TRUE: an officer; JUST FALSE: not an officer and not purporting to act as one (the "Where" fails);
              -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text) when the s 1261(1) answer is NOTHING ("includes": list not closed)

-- src:17886 | (2) Where an offence under this Part committed by a partnership is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of, or to be attributable to any neglect on the part of, a partner, he as well as the partnership is guilty of the offence and liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
@ref s 1255(2) Offences by partnerships: the partner (src:17886-17886)
GIVEN `the offence under this Part was committed by a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the offence was committed with the consent or connivance of the partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a partner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1255(2) the partner is guilty of the offence as well as the partnership` MEANS
    IF       `the offence under this Part was committed by a partnership`
         AND (`it is proved that the offence was committed with the consent or connivance of the partner`
              OR `it is proved that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the partner`)
         AND `the person is a partner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence under this Part committed by a partnership is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of, or to be attributable to any neglect on the part of, a partner"

-- src:17887 | (3) Where an offence under this Part committed by an unincorporated association (other than a partnership) is proved to have been committed with the consent or connivance of, or to be attributable to any neglect on the part of, any officer of the association or any member of its governing body, he as well as the association is guilty of the offence and liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
@ref s 1255(3) Offences by unincorporated associations: officer or member of the governing body (src:17887-17887)
GIVEN `the offence under this Part was committed by an unincorporated association (other than a partnership)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the offence was committed with the consent or connivance of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is proved that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an officer of the association or a member of its governing body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1255(3) the officer or member is guilty of the offence as well as the association` MEANS
    IF       `the offence under this Part was committed by an unincorporated association (other than a partnership)`
         AND (`it is proved that the offence was committed with the consent or connivance of the person`
              OR `it is proved that the offence is attributable to any neglect on the part of the person`)
         AND `the person is an officer of the association or a member of its governing body`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence under this Part committed by an unincorporated association (other than a partnership) is proved"

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1256 Time limits for prosecution of offences
-- =========================================================================================================

-- "the period of twelve months beginning with the date": ends the day before the corresponding date a year later. When
-- the corresponding date does not exist (a start on 29 February), the period ends on the last day of February (fork F-C).
-- src:17889 | (1) An information relating to an offence under this Part which is triable by a magistrates' court in England and Wales may be so tried if it is laid at any time within the period of twelve months beginning with the date on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State to justify the proceedings comes to his knowledge.
@ref s 1256(1) Time limits: twelve months beginning with the date (src:17889-17889)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 1256(1) the last day of the period of twelve months beginning with` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY (`add months` d 12) EQUALS DATE_DAY d
    THEN (`add months` d 12) MINUS 1
    ELSE `add months` d 12

@ref s 1256(1) Time limits: England and Wales (src:17889-17889)
GIVEN `the day the information was laid` IS A DATE
      `the day on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1256(1) the information may be tried in England and Wales` MEANS
    IF `the day the information was laid` AT MOST `s 1256(1) the last day of the period of twelve months beginning with` `the day on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions or the Secretary of State to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be so tried if it is laid at any time within the period of twelve months" (a period fixed in the text's own words: the ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))

-- src:17891 | (3) For the purposes of subsection (2) proceedings are to be deemed to be commenced on the date on which a warrant to apprehend or cite the accused is granted, if the warrant is executed without undue delay.
@ref s 1256(3) Time limits: proceedings deemed commenced (src:17891-17891)
GIVEN `the day a warrant to apprehend or cite the accused is granted` IS A DATE
      `the warrant is executed without undue delay` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 1256(3) the day on which the proceedings are deemed to be commenced` MEANS
    IF `the warrant is executed without undue delay`
    THEN JUST `the day a warrant to apprehend or cite the accused is granted`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if the warrant is executed without undue delay"

-- src:17890 | (2) Proceedings in Scotland for an offence under this Part may be commenced at any time within the period of twelve months beginning with the date on which evidence sufficient in the Lord Advocate's opinion to justify proceedings came to his knowledge or, where such evidence was reported to him by the Secretary of State, within the period of twelve months beginning with the date on which it came to the knowledge of the Secretary of State.
@ref s 1256(2) Time limits: Scotland (src:17890-17890)
GIVEN `the day the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day on which evidence sufficient in the Lord Advocate's opinion to justify proceedings came to his knowledge` IS A DATE
      `that evidence was reported to him by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it came to the knowledge of the Secretary of State` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1256(2) proceedings may be commenced in Scotland` MEANS
    IF       `the day the proceedings were commenced`
             AT MOST `s 1256(1) the last day of the period of twelve months beginning with` `the day on which evidence sufficient in the Lord Advocate's opinion to justify proceedings came to his knowledge`
         OR (    `that evidence was reported to him by the Secretary of State`
             AND `the day the proceedings were commenced`
                 AT MOST `s 1256(1) the last day of the period of twelve months beginning with` `the day it came to the knowledge of the Secretary of State`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be commenced at any time within the period of twelve months beginning with the date" (a period fixed in the text's own words)

-- src:17892 | (4) A complaint charging an offence under this Part which is triable by a magistrates' court in Northern Ireland may be so tried if it is made at any time within the period of twelve months beginning with the date on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State to justify the proceedings comes to his knowledge.
@ref s 1256(4) Time limits: Northern Ireland (src:17892-17892)
GIVEN `the day the complaint was made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1256(4) the complaint may be tried in Northern Ireland` MEANS
    IF `the day the complaint was made` AT MOST `s 1256(1) the last day of the period of twelve months beginning with` `the day on which evidence sufficient in the opinion of the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State to justify the proceedings came to his knowledge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "may be so tried if it is made at any time within the period of twelve months" (a period fixed in the text's own words)

-- src:17893 | (5) This section does not authorise—
-- src:17894 | (a) in the case of proceedings in England and Wales, the trial of an information laid,
-- src:17895 | (b) in the case of proceedings in Scotland, the commencement of proceedings, or
-- src:17896 | (c) in the case of proceedings in Northern Ireland, the trial of a complaint made,
-- src:17897 | more than three years after the commission of the offence.
@ref s 1256(5) Time limits: three years from the offence (src:17893-17897)
GIVEN `the day the offence was committed` IS A DATE
      `the day the information was laid, the proceedings were commenced or the complaint was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1256(5) this section authorises the trial or the commencement` MEANS
    IF `the day the information was laid, the proceedings were commenced or the complaint was made` GREATER THAN (`add years` `the day the offence was committed` 3)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section does not authorise ... more than three years after the commission of the offence"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (5) only takes authority away; within three years the authority comes from subsections (1), (2) and (4)

-- src:17898 | (6) For the purposes of this section a certificate of the Director of Public Prosecutions, the Lord Advocate, the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State as to the date on which such evidence as is referred to above came to his knowledge is conclusive evidence.
@ref s 1256(6) Time limits: certificate (src:17898-17898)
GIVEN `a certificate of the Director of Public Prosecutions, the Lord Advocate, the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State states the date on which such evidence came to his knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1256(6) the certificate is conclusive evidence of that date` MEANS
    IF `a certificate of the Director of Public Prosecutions, the Lord Advocate, the Director of Public Prosecutions for Northern Ireland or the Secretary of State states the date on which such evidence came to his knowledge`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a certificate of the Director of Public Prosecutions, the Lord Advocate ... as to the date"

-- src:17899 | (7) Nothing in this section affects proceedings within the time limits prescribed by section 127(1) of the Magistrates' Courts Act 1980 (c. 43), section 331 of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1975 or Article 19 of the Magistrates' Courts (Northern Ireland) Order 1981 (S.I. 1981/1675 (N.I. 26)) (the usual time limits for criminal proceedings).
@ref s 1256(7) Time limits: the usual time limits (src:17899-17899)
GIVEN `the proceedings are within the time limits prescribed by section 127(1) of the Magistrates' Courts Act 1980, section 331 of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1975 or Article 19 of the Magistrates' Courts (Northern Ireland) Order 1981` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1256(7) this section affects the proceedings` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are within the time limits prescribed by section 127(1) of the Magistrates' Courts Act 1980, section 331 of the Criminal Procedure (Scotland) Act 1975 or Article 19 of the Magistrates' Courts (Northern Ireland) Order 1981`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section affects proceedings within the time limits prescribed by"
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording)

-- =========================================================================================================
-- s 1257 Jurisdiction and procedure in respect of offences
-- =========================================================================================================

DECLARE `s 1257(1) kind of defendant` IS ONE OF
    `s 1257(1)(a) a body corporate or unincorporated association`
    `s 1257(1)(b) an individual`

-- src:17901 | (1) Summary proceedings for an offence under this Part may, without prejudice to any jurisdiction exercisable apart from this section, be taken—
-- src:17902 | (a) against a body corporate or unincorporated association at any place at which it has a place of business, and
-- src:17903 | (b) against an individual at any place where he is for the time being.
@ref s 1257(1) Jurisdiction: where summary proceedings may be taken (src:17901-17903)
GIVEN kind IS A `s 1257(1) kind of defendant`
      `the body has a place of business at the place` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is for the time being at the place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1257(1) summary proceedings may be taken at the place` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `s 1257(1)(a) a body corporate or unincorporated association` THEN
        IF `the body has a place of business at the place`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without prejudice to any jurisdiction exercisable apart from this section"
    WHEN `s 1257(1)(b) an individual` THEN
        IF `the individual is for the time being at the place`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "without prejudice to any jurisdiction exercisable apart from this section"

-- src:17904 | (2) Proceedings for an offence alleged to have been committed under this Part by an unincorporated association must be brought in the name of the association (and not in that of any of its members), and for the purposes of any such proceedings any rules of court relating to the service of documents apply as in relation to a body corporate.
@ref s 1257(2) Jurisdiction: proceedings against an unincorporated association (src:17904-17904)
GIVEN `the proceedings are brought in the name of the association (and not in that of any of its members)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 1257(2) the proceedings against the unincorporated association are brought as the section requires` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are brought in the name of the association (and not in that of any of its members)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be brought in the name of the association (and not in that of any of its members)" (a bare "must" not done: fork F-D)

-- src:17905 | (3) Section 33 of the Criminal Justice Act 1925 (c. 86) and Schedule 3 to the Magistrates' Courts Act 1980 (c. 43) (procedure on charge of offence against a corporation) apply in a case in which an unincorporated association is charged in England and Wales with an offence under this Part as they apply in the case of a corporation.
-- src:17906 | (4) Section 18 of the Criminal Justice Act (Northern Ireland) 1945 (c. 15 (N.I.)) and Article 166 and Schedule 4 to the Magistrates' Courts (Northern Ireland) Order 1981 (S.I. 1981/1675 (N.I. 26)) (procedure on charge of offence against a corporation) apply in a case in which an unincorporated association is charged in Northern Ireland with an offence under this Part as they apply in the case of a corporation.
